<idea-plugin>
    <id>com.fitdeveloper.plugin</id>
    <name>FitDeveloper</name>
    <vendor>FitDeveloper (42AD x JetBrains hackathon)</vendor>
    <description><![CDATA[
    <p><b>FitDeveloper — walk to unlock your IDE.</b></p>
    <p>An always-on engine inside the IDE tracks REAL editor keystrokes and fills
    the crunch meter while you code. When sustained typing is detected the IDE
    itself <b>forces a walking break</b>: a QR code appears, your phone counts
    steps (DeviceMotion pedometer), progress syncs live through the plugin's
    built-in relay server — no Node.js, no external tools. Completing the walk
    unlocks the IDE with "Crunch Break Verified! +100 Mana".</p>
    <p>Configure it under <b>Settings | Tools | FitDeveloper</b>: disable/enable
    the forced-break engine without uninstalling, freely set how many seconds
    of sustained typing trigger a break, and freely set the step target.
    Every value is editable and applies instantly — no restart needed.</p>
    <p>This is the <b>IDE plugin</b> variant of FitDeveloper — it runs in both
    <b>IntelliJ IDEA</b> and <b>Android Studio</b> (any 2024.2+ based IDE).
    The standalone variant (runs in a normal browser with a Node server) lives
    in the <code>without-plugin</code> folder of the same repository, kept
    under its original prototype name "CrunchGuard".</p>
    ]]></description>

    <depends>com.intellij.modules.platform</depends>

    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.intellij">
        <toolWindow id="FitDeveloper"
                    anchor="right"
                    factoryClass="com.fitdeveloper.plugin.FitDeveloperToolWindowFactory"
                    icon="/web/icon.svg"/>
        <notificationGroup id="FitDeveloper" displayType="BALLOON"/>
        <postStartupActivity implementation="com.fitdeveloper.plugin.FitDeveloperStartup"/>
        <applicationConfigurable parentId="tools"
                                 id="com.fitdeveloper.plugin.settings"
                                 displayName="FitDeveloper"
                                 instance="com.fitdeveloper.plugin.FitDeveloperSettings"/>
    </extensions>
</idea-plugin>
